  "eventSemantics": {
    "down": "Physical button/pad activation; a delayed hold action may arm here and fire later according to its binding lifecycle.",
    "up": "Physical button/pad release. Required hold modifiers are inspected at this edge unless a binding documents a stored ownership latch.",
    "turn": "Encoder movement carrying signed detents; it has no implicit down/up lifecycle.",
    "shift": "Effective Shift, including sticky behavior, except entries explicitly requiring physical Shift.",
    "midi": "Legacy catalog MIDI event suffixes denote received messages, not local button edges. CC.down does not by itself imply nonzero value or a threshold crossing; each binding's when clause defines its eligibility.",
    "wildcards": "button and pad identify incoming event families. They are not extra physical controls."
  },
